# Laravel backend

## Structure

- Controllers in `app/Http/Controllers/Api/`: thin, JSON only (SRP: no QBO SDK, no heavy business rules).
- Services in `app/Services/`: `Service` suffix, business logic and QBO (sole SDK access point).
- Routes in `routes/api.php`, `/api` prefix.
- DRY: all QBO/OAuth/token logic lives in `QuickBooksService`; JSON `error` codes reused by the frontend via `getApiErrorMessage`.

## QuickBooks

- SDK: `quickbooks/v3-php-sdk` via `QuickBooksService`.
- OAuth tokens: `QuickBooksToken` model, `quickbooks_tokens` table.
- Do not pass `null` to QBO refs (e.g. omit `CustomerRef` when absent).
- JSON error codes: `error` (e.g. `quickbooks_not_connected`, `registration_disabled`).
- `ALLOW_REGISTRATION` controls public registration; `QUICKBOOKS_EXPOSE_API_ERRORS` filters Intuit details.

## Tests (required)

```php
// Feature test with mock
$this->mock(QuickBooksService::class, function ($mock) { ... });

// Scope for mutation testing
covers(TimeActivityController::class);
```

- Feature: `tests/Feature/`
- Unit: `tests/Unit/` (e.g. mock session/Auth for `AuthController::logout`)
- Arch: `tests/Arch/`
- Gherkin: `features/api/*.feature`
- Minimum coverage: **85 %** (`composer test:coverage`, QBO finance standard)
- Mutation: **Pest `--mutate`** score ≥ 80 % (`composer test:mutation`)
- `app/Services/QuickBooksService.php`: aim for **100 %** (OAuth + tokens core)

## Style

- `composer format` (Laravel Pint preset) before commit.
- `composer phpcs`: required PHPDoc on `app/` (see `.cursor/rules/phpdoc.mdc`).
- `composer lint`: Pint + PHPCS (called by root `npm run lint`).
- PHPStan level 5: `composer analyse`.
